# ADR 008: Prompt Injection Defense Strategy

## Status
Accepted (Updated from Rebuff)

## Context
Originally planned to use `rebuff` library for prompt injection detection, but:
- Library has minimal recent maintenance
- Limited TypeScript support
- Adds external dependency for critical security feature

## Decision

**Use custom pattern-based detection instead of Rebuff.**

### Multi-Layer Defense

```typescript
interface InjectionDetectionResult {
  isInjection: boolean;
  confidence: number;        // 0-1
  detectedPatterns: string[];
  sanitizedContent?: string;
}

class PromptInjectionDetector {
  private patterns: RegExp[] = [
    // Direct instruction override
    /ignore\s+(all\s+)?(previous|above|prior)\s+instructions?/i,
    /disregard\s+(all\s+)?(previous|above|prior)\s+instructions?/i,
    /forget\s+(everything|all)\s+(you\s+)?know/i,

    // Role manipulation
    /you\s+are\s+(now|actually)\s+a/i,
    /pretend\s+(to\s+be|you'?re)/i,
    /act\s+as\s+(if|though)/i,

    // System prompt extraction
    /what\s+(is|are)\s+your\s+(system\s+)?instructions?/i,
    /show\s+me\s+your\s+(system\s+)?prompt/i,
    /repeat\s+(back\s+)?(your|the)\s+instructions/i,

    // Delimiter attacks
    /```\s*(system|assistant|user)\s*\n/i,
    /<\/?system>/i,
    /\[INST\]/i,

    // Data exfiltration
    /send\s+(this\s+)?(to|via)\s+(my\s+)?email/i,
    /upload\s+(this\s+)?to/i,
    /http:\/\/|https:\/\/[^\s]+\.(tk|ml|ga|cf|gq)/i,  // Suspicious TLDs
  ];

  detect(content: string): InjectionDetectionResult {
    const detected: string[] = [];
    let confidence = 0;

    for (const pattern of this.patterns) {
      if (pattern.test(content)) {
        detected.push(pattern.source);
        confidence = Math.min(1, confidence + 0.3);
      }
    }

    return {
      isInjection: detected.length > 0,
      confidence,
      detectedPatterns: detected,
    };
  }
}
```

