# Offline-First Design

Hikaflow should degrade gracefully when services are unavailable.

## Service Dependencies

| Service | Required For | Offline Fallback |
|---------|--------------|------------------|
| Anthropic API | Agent chat | Ollama local LLM |
| OpenAI API | Agent chat (alt) | Ollama local LLM |
| Sentry API | Production correlation | Skip, local-only signals |
| GitHub API | PR integration | Skip, local-only |
| Network | All external | Full offline mode |

## Offline Capabilities

### Always Available (No Network)
- DependencyGraph building (ts-morph, local)
- All static analyzers (impact, breaking change, etc.)
- All observers (boundary, fragility, etc.)
- Signal system (local state)
- CodeLens display
- Cache (LRU, local)
- Git operations (local repo)

### Requires LLM (Cloud or Local)
- Agent chat
- Signal explanations (detailed)
- Fix suggestions
- Code generation

### Requires Cloud Only
- Sentry error correlation
- GitHub PR comments
- Remote telemetry

## Graceful Degradation

### When Anthropic/OpenAI Unavailable

```typescript
class ModelRouter {
  async selectModel(task: AgentTask): Promise<ModelConfig> {
    // Try cloud providers first
    if (await this.isAvailable('anthropic')) {
      return this.anthropicConfig;
    }
    if (await this.isAvailable('openai')) {
      return this.openaiConfig;
    }

    // Fall back to Ollama
    if (await this.isAvailable('ollama')) {
      return this.ollamaConfig;
    }

    // No LLM available
    throw new OfflineModeError('No LLM available. Install Ollama for offline mode.');
  }

  private async isAvailable(provider: string): Promise<boolean> {
    try {
      await this.ping(provider);
      return true;
    } catch {
      return false;
    }
  }
}
```

### When Sentry Unavailable

```typescript
class SentryIntegration {
  private available = false;

  async initialize(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      await this.testConnection();
      this.available = true;
    } catch {
      console.log('Sentry unavailable, production correlation disabled');
      this.available = false;
    }
  }

  async correlateErrors(file: string): Promise<RuntimeError[]> {
    if (!this.available) {
      return [];  // Graceful degradation - empty results
    }
    return this.fetchErrors(file);
  }
}
```

