## Important Limitations

**SWC CANNOT detect type-based issues.** It only strips types without checking them.

### SWC CAN detect:
- Syntax errors
- Import/export structure (names only, not types)
- Function/class/variable counts
- Cyclomatic complexity (structural)
- Unreachable code

### SWC CANNOT detect:
- Type narrowing issues
- Generic constraint violations
- Cross-file type dependencies
- Breaking changes in signatures (needs AccurateAnalyzer)
- Unused types (only unused values)
- Whether an export is actually used by importers

**Use AccurateAnalyzer (task 016) for anything requiring type information.**

